    "AXHelp=Individual track zoom. Drag the track’s bottom divider line to adjust its vertical track zoom level. Command-drag to adjust all tracks of the same track type. Shift-click to reset all tracks to the default zoom level. ",
    "AXHelp=Input Monitoring button. Hear incoming signals on audio or software instrument tracks that aren’t record enabled. This is useful when setting levels or practicing parts before recording. ",
    "AXHelp=Mute button. Silence a track’s signal, audibly removing it from project playback. Corresponds to the Mute button on the channel strip in the Mixer, so that changing one also changes the other. ",
    "AXHelp=Name field. Double-click to rename the track. ",
    "AXHelp=Pan\/Balance knob. Drag vertically to position the track signal in the stereo field. ",
    "AXHelp=Record Enable button. Prepare the track for recording, or deactivate a record-ready track. The button changes to indicate whether the track is inactive, record enabled, or currently recording. ",
    "AXHelp=Solo button. Isolate a track’s signal so that it can be heard without other tracks. Use on an aux or output channel strip to isolate that part of the mix. ",
    "AXHelp=Track header. Mute or solo the track’s channel strip signal, enable the track for recording, and adjust volume or pan. Control-click and choose Track Header Components to select which controls to show or hide. ",
    "AXHelp=Volume fader. Set a track’s playback volume. Use on an aux or output channel strip to adjust the volume of that part of the mix, or on the output channel strip to set the overall project volume. ",
